"will sign our drivers with a publicly verifiable certificate. However, it "
"should be noted that even given the fact that those drivers are not "
"digitally signed, this doesn't affect the security of the Windows VM in any "
"way. This is because the actual installation `iso` file can be verified as "
"described in step 3 below. The only downside of those drivers not being "
"signed is the inconvenience to the user that he or she must disable the "
"signature enforcement policy before installing the tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:151
