msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:207
#: bbdc4dfdf2d240f5b64001179ab4cc04
msgid "Installing Qubes Windows Tools (QWT) in a Windows VM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:210
#: e15ef3ed71df4adb817822447fb5c5ac
msgid ""
"Installing the Qubes Windows Tools on Windows 7, 10, and 11, both as a "
"StandaloneVM as well as a Template VM and a corresponding AppVM, is "
"described in the following sections."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:212
#: 7f5c285f665f435780c619f2e1fb70ad
msgid ""
"**Note:** Seamless mode is currently only available in an experimental "
"version for Windows 10 and 11. Please check the top of this document for the "
"full feature availability breakdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:217
#: 4bee750ab0ef427da30eaddd695b5024
msgid ""
"For Qubes R4.2, the new version of QWT is not included in the repositories, "
"but it can be downloaded from the R4.3 repository (version `4.2.2-1 <https://"
"yum.qubes-os.org/r4.3/current-testing/dom0/fc41/rpm/qubes-windows-"
"tools-4.2.2-1.fc41.noarch.rpm>`__ ), and it will work under R4.2, too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:220
#: 37ec8ac86094495e9531cb653c902f19
msgid ""
"First, make sure that ``qubes-windows-tools`` is installed in your system:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:222
#: 583afeafcd0643f3be660fc254991ea8
msgid ""
"For use with **Windows 7**, install the previous version of Qubes Windows "
"Tools. The corresponding .rpm file for manual QWT installation for Windows "
"7is still available from the repositories for Qubes R4.2 (version `4.1.69-1 "
"<https://yum.qubes-os.org/r4.2/current/dom0/fc37/rpm/qubes-windows-"
"tools-4.1.69-1.fc37.noarch.rpm>`__ )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:224
#: 6e49fcbdd44c4d6a99062970adbcd2d4
msgid ""
"After downloading, copy the file to `dom0` as described in `How to copy from "
"dom0 <https://www.qubes-os.org/doc/how-to-copy-from-dom0/#copying-to-"
"dom0>`__ and install it via ``sudo dnf install PATH_TO_RPMFILE``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:226
#: 222fefcde19a4849a5553004503072a1
msgid ""
"For use with **Windows 10 and 11**, you have to install the new version "
"4.2.2 of Qubes Windows Tools. In Qubes R4.3, the QWT package is already part "
"of the repositories. So, QWT can be installed directy, without downloading "
"anything, via"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:233
#: 705d02beb8f642359ab05fe5eed2d57b
msgid ""
"**Caution:** Installing one of these QWT versions will remove the other if "
"it is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:235
#: db3b8c20f8a6447eaa7d7596efb314d8
msgid ""
"**Warning:** In Windows 7, the older version of Qubes Windows Tools will be "
"replaced during the next ``dom0`` update by the current dummy version "
"4.1.70-1. This can be inhibited by appending the line ``exclude=qubes-"
"windows-tools`` to the file ``/etc/dnf/dnf.conf`` in ``dom0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:237
#: 68d25167052c423782601279841399ee
msgid ""
"This package makes the ISO with Qubes Windows Tools available, which is "
"passed to the VM when ``--install-windows-tools`` is specified for the ``qvm-"
"start`` command. Please note that none of this software ever runs in "
"``dom0`` or any other part of the system except for the Windows AppVM in "
"which it is to be installed. (It could not run in ``dom0`` at all, because "
"``dom0`` is a VM running under Fedora, while the QWT software is Windows "
"software.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:239
#: e26e5f019c434355b1f8a60d8c9c8d8d
msgid ""
"To install the Qubes Windows Tools in a Windows VM, one should start the VM "
"passing the additional option ``--install-windows-tools``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:245
#: e6c711ecca9c4df99cf89b05da5be1ec
msgid ""
"Once the Windows VM boots, a CDROM should appear in the ‘My Computer’ menu "
"(typically as ``D:`` or ``E:``) with the setup program with the setup "
"program ``qubes-tools-x64.msi`` for Windows 7 or ``qubes-tools-4.2.2.exe`` "
"for Windows 10 and 11 in its main directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:247
#: d29339150ca44362aeec2bacf613e270
msgid ""
"Install Qubes Windows Tools by starting the setup program (logged in as "
"administrator), optionally selecting the ``Xen PV disk drivers``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:249
#: 29da600883a4411d84cced91ba342d93
msgid ""
"**Caution:** For Windows 7, the installation of the graphics driver in the "
"first step will probably break the Windows qube, causing it to show only a "
"black window and become unresponsive; the graphics driver has to be "
"installed later on in a second step described below. For Windows 10 and 11, "
"the Qubes graphics driver is still in experimental development. It may work "
"or not, possibly depending on your hardware. So, in Windows 10 and 11, it "
"may be less risky to install Qubes Windows Tools without selecting this "
"driver, and later on, to try it in a clone of your Windows VM by re-running "
"the installation in change mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:251
#: fd21570405a546599ed5253f798f2d16
msgid ""
"**Warning:** The installation of the PV disk drivers may lead Windows to "
"declare that the hardware has changed and that, in consequence, the "
"activation is no longer valid, possibly complaining that the use of the "
"software is no longer lawful. It should be possible to reactivate the "
"software if a valid product key is provided."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/templates/windows/qubes-windows-tools.rst:253
#: 355bf24cd942427bb31af3a33b5b6447
msgid ""
"For installation in a template, you should select ``Move user profiles``."
